<h1>Frequently Asked Questions</h1>

<div class="faq">
  <details name="faq">
    <summary>What is CSBFP?</summary>
    <p>Certified Small Business Finance Professional (CSBFP) is a professional certification for individuals working in commercial finance. It confirms completion of industry training, a passing assessment, a one-time background check, and agreement to professional standards.</p>
  </details>
  <details name="faq">
    <summary>Who can get certified?</summary>
    <p>Anyone 18 or older working in commercial finance. Current employment is not required.</p>
    <p>We especially encourage professionals at brokerages and lenders who are involved in the financing process, including sales, management, underwriting, processing, funding, servicing, operations, compliance, and risk.</p>
  </details>
  <details name="faq">
    <summary>What are the steps?</summary>
    <p>Create an account, complete your application and training modules, pass the assessment, and pay the annual fee. You'll then receive an invitation to complete a one-time background check. Allow 1–3 days for results. Your certification number will be issued upon approval.</p>
  </details>
  <details name="faq">
    <summary>Can certification requirements change?</summary>
    <p>Yes. CSBFP may update its training, assessments, and certification requirements to reflect changes in the industry, regulations, and professional standards. Certified individuals will be notified of any new requirements and given reasonable time to complete them.</p>
  </details>
  <details name="faq">
    <summary>What information do I need?</summary>
    <p>Your legal name, date of birth, home ZIP code, email and mobile number, your current employer and role (if you have one), and the financing products you work with.</p>
  </details>
  <details name="faq">
    <summary>What does the training involve?</summary>
    <p>Four short modules (Fundamentals, Products &amp; Terminology, Federal &amp; State Regulation, and Professional Conduct) followed by a 20-question multiple-choice assessment. You need 80% (16 of 20) to pass, and you can save your progress and come back. You have up to 10 attempts, with a 60-minute wait between them.</p>
  </details>
  <details name="faq">
    <summary>Is there a background check?</summary>
    <p>Yes. All applicants undergo a one-time background check through Checkr. Convictions involving financial crimes or fraud within the past seven years may affect eligibility.</p>
  </details>
  <details name="faq">
    <summary>How much does it cost?</summary>
    <p><%= program.annualFee %> per year, paid by credit or debit card after passing the assessment and before your background check is initiated.</p>
  </details>
  <details name="faq">
    <summary>Can my employer pay?</summary>
    <p>Yes. Employers can buy certification credits on the <a href="/employers">For Employers</a> page. Ask your employer for their Employer ID and enter it at the payment step. An employer credit covers your first year; after that, you can keep your certification active by adding your own card.</p>
  </details>
  <details name="faq">
    <summary>Can I get a refund?</summary>
    <p>The <%= program.annualFee %> annual certification fee is non-refundable once paid, including if you do not pass the background check, except where required by law.</p>
  </details>
  <details name="faq">
    <summary>Does it renew automatically?</summary>
    <p>Yes. Your certification renews every 12 months at <%= program.annualFee %>. We'll email you 30 days before renewal, and you can cancel future renewals online at any time. You do not need to repeat the background check or assessment.</p>
  </details>
  <details name="faq">
    <summary>What if I change jobs?</summary>
    <p>Your certification belongs to you, not your employer. Your certification number stays the same throughout your career. You can update your employer information from your account at any time.</p>
  </details>
  <details name="faq">
    <summary>Can a certification be suspended or revoked?</summary>
    <p>Yes. Certifications may be suspended or revoked for material misrepresentation, misconduct, or violations of program standards. You will be notified and given an opportunity to respond. Public verification displays only your certification status, not the reason for suspension or revocation.</p>
  </details>
</div>

<div class="actions">
  <a class="button" href="/portal/signup">Get Certified</a>
  <a class="button secondary" href="/support">Ask a Question</a>
</div>
<%- include('partials/foot') %>
